{{also|sadā}}
==Crimean Gothic==

===Etymology===
Probably from an Eastern Iranian ({{etyl|xsc|gme-cgo}}) language. Compare Avestan {{m|ae|𐬯𐬀𐬙𐬀|tr=sata}}, Ossetian {{m|os|сӕдӕ|tr=sædæ}}.

===Numeral===
{{head|gme-cgo|numeral}}

# [[hundred]]
#* 1562, Ogier Ghiselin de Busbecq:
#*: Viginti dicebat stega, triginta treithyen, quadraginta furdeithien, centum '''sada''', hazer mille.

