==Estonian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|et|fiu-fin-pro|*sata}}, from {{inh|et|fiu-pro|*śata||hundred}}. Cognates include Hungarian {{m|hu|száz}} and Finnish {{m|fi|sata}}. Originally borrowed from an {{etyl|iir|et}} language; compare Avestan {{m|ae|𐬯𐬀𐬙𐬀|tr=sata}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|शत|tr=śatá}}.

